    "text": "This is a greedy heuristic. I have not run it against the actual data sets, so I can't give scores.\n\n**Approach**\n1. **Coverage.** For each router position, the covered cells are found quadrant by quadrant. Moving away from the router row by row, the allowed column reach can only shrink. A wall cuts off everything beyond it in that row and in all rows further out.\n2. **Choosing routers.** Each non-wall cell is a candidate, ranked by `newly covered target cells / (Pr + Pb \u00b7 d)`. Here `d` is the number of backbone cells needed to reach the nearest existing backbone cell.\n3. **Lazy greedy.** Candidates sit in a priority queue. When the top entry is popped, its gain and distance are recomputed; it is accepted if it is still the best, and pushed back otherwise. Coverage gain can only go down, so stored keys stay valid upper bounds. Whenever a cell's distance to the backbone drops, a fresh entry is pushed for it.\n4. **Backbone.** A breadth-first search over the 8-neighbour grid keeps, for every cell, its distance to the current backbone and a parent pointer. Walls do not block cables, so this is the Chebyshev distance. When a router is accepted, the parent chain is followed back to the backbone. That path is added in an order where each cell comes after a neighbour, and the search is then updated only where distances get shorter.\n5. **Budget.** A router is placed only if its exact cost (router plus path) fits in the remaining budget. The loop stops when no router can be afforded or nothing uncovered is left.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint H, W, R;\nvector<char> g;\nvector<char> covered;\n\ntemplate<class F>\nvoid forCov(int a, int b, F f) {\n    for (int s = 1; s >= -1; s -= 2)\n        for (int t = 1; t >= -1; t -= 2) {\n            int lim = R;\n            for (int k = 0; k <= R; k++) {\n                int x = a + s * k;\n                if (x < 0 || x >= H) break;\n                int j = 0;\n                while (j <= lim) {\n                    int y = b + t * j;\n                    if (y < 0 || y >= W || g[x * W + y] == '#') break;\n                    if ((k > 0 || s == 1) && (j > 0 || t == 1)) f(x * W + y);\n                    j++;\n                }\n                lim = j - 1;\n                if (lim < 0) break;\n            }\n        }\n}\n\nint gainOf(int c) {\n    int a = c / W, b = c % W;\n    int cnt = 0;\n    forCov(a, b, [&](int id) { if (g[id] == '.' && !covered[id]) cnt++; });\n    return cnt;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    long long Pb, Pr, B;\n    int br, bc;\n    cin >> H >> W >> R;\n    cin >> Pb >> Pr >> B;\n    cin >> br >> bc;\n    int N = H * W;\n    g.assign(N, '-');\n    for (int i = 0; i < H; i++) {\n        string s;\n        cin >> s;\n        for (int j = 0; j < W && j < (int)s.size(); j++) g[i * W + j] = s[j];\n    }\n    covered.assign(N, 0);\n    vector<char> isRouter(N, 0), isBack(N, 0);\n    vector<int> dist(N, INT_MAX), par(N, -1);\n    int src = br * W + bc;\n    isBack[src] = 1;\n    dist[src] = 0;\n    {\n        vector<int> q;\n        q.reserve(N);\n        q.push_back(src);\n        for (size_t qi = 0; qi < q.size(); qi++) {\n            int u = q[qi];\n            int ux = u / W, uy = u % W;\n            for (int dx = -1; dx <= 1; dx++)\n                for (int dy = -1; dy <= 1; dy++) {\n                    if (!dx && !dy) continue;\n                    int nx = ux + dx, ny = uy + dy;\n                    if (nx < 0 || ny < 0 || nx >= H || ny >= W) continue;\n                    int n = nx * W + ny;\n                    if (dist[n] > dist[u] + 1) {\n                        dist[n] = dist[u] + 1;\n                        par[n] = u;\n                        q.push_back(n);\n                    }\n                }\n        }\n    }\n    vector<int> lastGain(N, 0);\n    priority_queue<pair<double, int>> pq;\n    for (int c = 0; c < N; c++) {\n        if (g[c] == '#') continue;\n        int gg = gainOf(c);\n        lastGain[c] = gg;\n        if (gg > 0) pq.push({gg / (double)(Pr + Pb * dist[c]), c});\n    }\n    long long remaining = B;\n    vector<int> backList, routers;\n    vector<int> bq;\n    while (!pq.empty() && remaining >= Pr) {\n        auto [k, c] = pq.top();\n        pq.pop();\n        if (isRouter[c]) continue;\n        int gnow = gainOf(c);\n        lastGain[c] = gnow;\n        if (gnow == 0) continue;\n        double key = gnow / (double)(Pr + Pb * dist[c]);\n        if (!pq.empty() && key < pq.top().first - 1e-12) {\n            pq.push({key, c});\n            continue;\n        }\n        // build path\n        vector<int> path;\n        int u = c;\n        while (!isBack[u]) { path.push_back(u); u = par[u]; }\n        long long cost = Pr + Pb * (long long)path.size();\n        if (cost > remaining) continue;\n        remaining -= cost;\n        reverse(path.begin(), path.end());\n        bq.clear();\n        for (int p : path) {\n            backList.push_back(p);\n            isBack[p] = 1;\n            dist[p] = 0;\n            bq.push_back(p);\n        }\n        isRouter[c] = 1;\n        routers.push_back(c);\n        forCov(c / W, c % W, [&](int id) { covered[id] = 1; });\n        // incremental BFS\n        for (size_t qi = 0; qi < bq.size(); qi++) {\n            int v = bq[qi];\n            int vx = v / W, vy = v % W;\n            for (int dx = -1; dx <= 1; dx++)\n                for (int dy = -1; dy <= 1; dy++) {\n                    if (!dx && !dy) continue;\n                    int nx = vx + dx, ny = vy + dy;\n                    if (nx < 0 || ny < 0 || nx >= H || ny >= W) continue;\n                    int n = nx * W + ny;\n                    if (dist[n] > dist[v] + 1) {\n                        dist[n] = dist[v] + 1;\n                        par[n] = v;\n                        bq.push_back(n);\n                        if (g[n] != '#' && !isRouter[n] && lastGain[n] > 0)\n                            pq.push({lastGain[n] / (double)(Pr + Pb * dist[n]), n});\n                    }\n                }\n        }\n        // also router cells on path with dist 0 may be candidates: push them\n        for (int p : path) {\n            if (g[p] != '#' && !isRouter[p] && lastGain[p] > 0)\n                pq.push({lastGain[p] / (double)(Pr), p});\n        }\n    }\n    string out;\n    out.reserve((backList.size() + routers.size()) * 12 + 32);\n    out += to_string(backList.size());\n    out += '\\n';\n    for (int p : backList) {\n        out += to_string(p / W);\n        out += ' ';\n        out += to_string(p % W);\n        out += '\\n';\n    }\n    out += to_string(routers.size());\n    out += '\\n';\n    for (int p : routers) {\n        out += to_string(p / W);\n        out += ' ';\n        out += to_string(p % W);\n        out += '\\n';\n    }\n    fwrite(out.data(), 1, out.size(), stdout);\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
